      "tagline": "One first frame, 20.75 seconds in a single take, sound included",
      "description": "A 20.75-second single take from one first frame, built as 3 H3 clips that continue each other: each clip starts from the previous clip's latent (picture and sound), not from saved frames. PROMPT FORMAT: shared text first, then one block per clip starting with [Shot 1], [Shot 2], ... each on its own line. Without [Shot] markers every clip gets the whole prompt. USE IT FOR one continuous shot of one scene that must run longer than 8 s, with the clip's own generated sound (for a performance to your own song, use the Music Video Chain instead). Put the reference line and the full scene in [Shot 1]; begin every later block with 'the existing camera motion and sound continue uninterrupted, do not restart' and describe only what happens next. Each later clip adds only 6.375 s: its first 1.625 s repeat the previous clip's end. EXPECT: picture gets softer by clip 3 (measured 0.72-0.83x of clip 1), then holds. Render time on a DGX Spark (GB10) at 544p, 7 steps: about 10 min (587 s measured; 3, 4 and 5 clips took 587, 780 and 985 s). The 480p draft tier took 450 s for 3 clips but is softer (edge 0.55x of 544p). Tested only on a DGX Spark (GB10, 128 GB unified memory); 12-16 GB cards and 32-64 GB RAM PCs are untested.",
